@startuml

title A lane cycle

hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

participant "Receive" as recv
queue "Ring buffer" as ring
participant "Lane worker" as lane
participant "Live fan-out" as live
database "Store" as db
participant "Consumers" as cons

recv -> ring : publish slot (sequence n)
note right of ring
    A full ring overwrites its oldest slot
    and counts the loss. The receiver never waits.
end note

lane -> ring : take every slot up to the cursor
ring --> lane : batch of k ticks

lane -> lane : age gate: drop a tick older than the limit of its class
lane -> lane : conflate: keep the newest tick of each datum

lane -> live : latest tick of each datum
live -> cons : publish on the party subject, no ack

alt the lag is below the first limit
    lane -> db : insert all kept ticks in one transaction
else the lag is above the first limit
    lane -> lane : keep the newest tick of each series for each second
    lane -> db : insert the kept ticks in one transaction
end

db --> lane : commit
lane -> lane : record the lag, the batch size and the commit time

@enduml
